    "plainEnglish": "This is a type of liver cancer that starts in the bile ducts inside the liver. Bile ducts are small tubes that carry bile (a digestive fluid) from the liver; when cancer develops in these ducts, it can block bile flow and damage liver function. People with this cancer may experience jaundice (yellowing of skin and eyes), abdominal pain, and weight loss.",
    "whoUses": "Oncologists, hepatologists, and general surgeons use this code when diagnosing and treating bile duct cancers. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients undergoing cancer treatment, imaging studies, or liver surgery consultations.",
