    "longDesc": "Sebaceous cell carcinoma of skin of right lower eyelid, including canthus",
    "plainEnglish": "Sebaceous cell carcinoma is a rare skin cancer that develops from oil glands in the skin, specifically on your right lower eyelid near the inner corner of your eye. This is an aggressive type of cancer that requires prompt treatment, as it can spread to nearby tissues and lymph nodes if left untreated. You may notice a persistent bump, nodule, or thickening on your eyelid that doesn't go away, or changes in the appearance of your eyelid.",
    "whoUses": "Ophthalmologists, dermatologists, and oculoplastic surgeons primarily diagnose and treat sebaceous cell carcinoma of the eyelid. This code commonly appears on patient EOBs when biopsies, surgical removal, or cancer treatment-related office visits and procedures are performed.",
