    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates you have basal cell carcinoma, a common type of skin cancer, located on the right ear or in the ear canal. Basal cell carcinoma grows slowly and is usually caused by long-term sun exposure; while it's the least aggressive form of skin cancer, it does need to be treated to prevent it from growing larger or spreading. You may have noticed a bump, sore, or unusual skin growth on or around your right ear that prompted your doctor to diagnose this condition.",
    "whoUses": "Dermatologists, otolaryngologists (ENT specialists), and oncologists use this code when treating skin cancer of the ear. It commonly appears on EOB statements as these are frequently biopsied and treated in outpatient settings, with the specific location (right ear) important for surgical planning and follow-up care.",
