    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates you have been diagnosed with cancer that started in the soft tissues of your trunk (the area between your neck and pelvis, including your chest, abdomen, and back). Soft tissue includes muscles, fat, nerves, and blood vessels, and when cancer develops in these areas, it's called a soft tissue sarcoma. The 'unspecified' part means your doctor has identified the cancer in this general location but may still be determining the exact type or doing further testing to pinpoint the specific tissue involved.",
    "whoUses": "Oncologists, surgical oncologists, and pathologists primarily use this code when diagnosing and treating soft tissue sarcomas. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients with newly diagnosed or confirmed trunk sarcomas, particularly in documentation from biopsy results, imaging reports, or initial cancer consultations.",
