    "longDesc": "Malignant neoplasm of overlapping sites of connective and soft tissue",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a type of cancer that starts in the soft tissues of your body—such as muscles, fat, tendons, or fibrous tissue—and affects more than one area at the same time. When a tumor spreads across multiple overlapping regions rather than staying in one distinct location, doctors use this code to capture that it's not confined to a single site. You may have noticed a lump, swelling, or discomfort in the affected area, and your doctor has determined through imaging or biopsy that this is a malignant (cancerous) tumor involving your connective tissues.",
