    "longDesc": "Malignant neoplasm of connective and soft tissue, unspecified",
    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates you have been diagnosed with cancer that started in soft tissues like muscles, fat, tendons, or fibrous connective tissue throughout your body, but the doctor hasn't yet specified exactly which type of soft tissue or where in your body it originated. Soft tissue sarcomas are relatively rare cancers that can develop anywhere in the body where these supportive tissues exist. Your medical team will likely order imaging tests and biopsies to pinpoint the exact location and type so they can plan the most effective treatment.",
    "whoUses": "Oncologists, surgical oncologists, and pathologists use this code during initial cancer diagnosis and workup when the specific location of soft tissue sarcoma has not yet been determined. It commonly appears on EOB statements as a temporary or preliminary diagnosis code that is typically replaced with a more specific code (like C49.1 for upper limb sarcoma or C49.2 for lower limb sarcoma) once imaging and pathology results clarify the tumor's exact location.",
