    "plainEnglish": "This code describes cancer of the penis when doctors haven't identified a more specific location or type of cancer. Penis cancer is a rare form of malignant tumor that can develop on the skin or tissues of the penis, and may present as unusual growths, sores, bleeding, or discoloration. The exact cause varies, but risk factors can include poor hygiene, certain infections (like HPV), and smoking.",
    "whoUses": "Urologists, oncologists, and general surgeons use this code when treating penile cancer patients. It commonly appears in hospital records and oncology billing, though less frequently on patient EOBs compared to other cancer types since penile cancer is relatively uncommon.",
