    "shortDesc": "Malignant neoplasm of spinal cord",
    "longDesc": "Malignant neoplasm of spinal cord",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes cancer that starts in the spinal cord, the bundle of nerve tissue that runs down the middle of your backbone and carries signals between your brain and the rest of your body. Spinal cord cancer is a serious condition where malignant (aggressive) cells grow in this critical nerve tissue, potentially causing pain, weakness, numbness, or loss of control over movement and bodily functions depending on where the cancer is located.",
    "whoUses": "Oncologists, neurosurgeons, and neurologists primarily use this code when diagnosing and treating spinal cord cancers. This code frequently appears on patient EOB statements for those undergoing chemotherapy, radiation therapy, or surgical treatment for spinal cord malignancies, as well as in imaging and pathology reports.",
