    "longDesc": "Malignant neoplasm of cauda equina",
    "plainEnglish": "A malignant (cancerous) tumor that develops in the cauda equina, which is a bundle of nerves at the bottom of the spinal cord that controls sensation and movement in the lower body, including the legs and bladder. This cancer can cause pain in the lower back or legs, weakness, numbness, loss of bladder or bowel control, and difficulty walking. These symptoms develop because the growing tumor compresses or damages the nerves in this area.",
    "whoUses": "Oncologists, neurosurgeons, and spine specialists use this code when diagnosing and treating primary spinal cord cancers. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients undergoing chemotherapy, radiation therapy, surgical intervention, or palliative care related to cauda equina malignancies.",
