    "shortDesc": "Malignant neoplasm of craniopharyngeal duct",
    "longDesc": "Malignant neoplasm of craniopharyngeal duct",
    "plainEnglish": "This is a cancer that develops in the craniopharyngeal duct, a small remnant tissue located at the base of the brain between the pituitary gland and the brain itself. These tumors grow from cells that should have disappeared during fetal development but sometimes persist into adulthood. When cancer develops here, it can grow and press on nearby brain structures, affecting hormone production, vision, and other brain functions.",
    "whoUses": "Neurosurgeons, neuro-oncologists, and endocrinologists typically diagnose and treat this condition, often using imaging studies like MRI. This code commonly appears on EOB statements for patients undergoing brain surgery, radiation therapy, or chemotherapy for craniopharyngeal duct cancer, which is a relatively rare type of brain tumor.",
