    "plainEnglish": "A carotid body tumor is a rare cancer that develops in a small cluster of nerve and blood vessel cells located in your neck where the carotid artery splits into two branches. These tumors grow in the tissue at the side of your neck and can press on nearby structures, potentially causing difficulty swallowing, hoarseness, or a visible lump. Most carotid body tumors grow slowly, but when they become cancerous (malignant), they can spread to other parts of the body and require aggressive treatment.",
