    "longDesc": "Malignant neoplasm associated with transplanted organ",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes cancer that develops in an organ after it has been transplanted into a patient's body. When someone receives a donated organ (like a kidney, liver, or heart), the cancer may have been present in that organ before transplantation, or it may develop afterward due to the immunosuppressive medications needed to prevent organ rejection. This is a serious complication because treating the cancer while protecting the transplanted organ requires careful medical management.",
    "whoUses": "Oncologists, transplant surgeons, and transplant specialists use this code when diagnosing and managing cancer in transplant recipients. It commonly appears on EOB statements for transplant patients who develop malignancies, as it helps coordinate care between cancer treatment and transplant management teams and ensures proper billing for the complex care required.",
    "billable": true,
    "isNew": false,
