    "longDesc": "Other types of follicular lymphoma, in remission",
    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates you have a less common form of follicular lymphoma (a slow-growing cancer of white blood cells called B lymphocytes in the lymph nodes) that is currently in remission, meaning the cancer is responding well to treatment and not actively progressing. Follicular lymphoma develops in the germinal centers of lymph nodes and typically grows slowly over time, though it can be difficult to cure completely. Being in remission means your cancer markers are improved, symptoms have subsided, or imaging shows no active disease—but your doctors will continue monitoring you regularly since remission doesn't always mean permanent cure.",
