    "shortDesc": "Subcutaneous panniculitis-like T-cell lymphoma, in remission",
    "longDesc": "Subcutaneous panniculitis-like T-cell lymphoma, in remission",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a rare type of blood cancer that forms in the fatty tissue under your skin, specifically a T-cell lymphoma that has responded to treatment and is currently in remission. In remission means the cancer is no longer actively growing or causing symptoms—it's under control, though your doctor will continue monitoring you to watch for any signs of the cancer returning. You may have experienced painful nodules or lumps under your skin before treatment, but these should have improved with therapy.",
    "whoUses": "Oncologists and hematologists use this code when documenting the status of patients with subcutaneous panniculitis-like T-cell lymphoma who are being followed after treatment. This code appears less frequently on patient EOB statements because it represents a rare cancer diagnosis, but it would be used during follow-up office visits, imaging studies, or laboratory monitoring to track remission status.",
