    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a rare cancer of the small intestine called immunoproliferative small intestinal disease (also known as alpha heavy chain disease) that is actively growing and has not gone away or improved with treatment. This condition involves abnormal immune cells multiplying in the small intestine, which can cause chronic diarrhea, weight loss, and malabsorption of nutrients. The 'not having achieved remission' part means the disease is either still present after treatment or has not responded adequately to therapy.",
    "whoUses": "This code is used by oncologists, hematologists, and gastroenterologists who diagnose and treat lymphomas and intestinal cancers. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients undergoing chemotherapy, biological therapy, or other cancer treatments, as well as for diagnostic procedures like endoscopy and biopsy.",
