    "whoUses": "Oncologists and hematologists use this code when documenting relapsed AML in patients undergoing chemotherapy, stem cell transplantation, or clinical trials. This code typically appears on EOB statements for cancer patients receiving inpatient hospital care, outpatient oncology treatment, or emergency visits related to leukemia complications, and it carries significant implications for insurance coverage and treatment authorization.",
