    "plainEnglish": "Acute panmyelosis with myelofibrosis is a rare and serious blood cancer where the bone marrow stops producing normal blood cells and becomes scarred (fibrotic), leading to severe shortages of red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. The \"in relapse\" part means the patient previously went into remission but the cancer has come back and is active again. Symptoms typically include severe anemia, infections due to low white blood cells, bleeding problems, and an enlarged spleen.",
    "whoUses": "This code is used by hematologists and oncologists treating patients with acute myeloid leukemias and myeloproliferative disorders in specialized hospital or cancer center settings. It commonly appears on EOBs for patients undergoing intensive chemotherapy, stem cell transplants, or clinical trial treatments, as this condition requires aggressive medical intervention.",
